# __PRODUCT_NAME__

A Harmos guest plugin exposing the local operation `greeting.greet`.
`operations/greeting/` owns the request, declaration and runtime implementation.
`domain/model/` owns shared greeting values and pure behavior. Disable default
features to use contracts alone; `runtime` enables execution and the carrier.

```sh
mise install
mise run prepare
cargo generate-lockfile
mise run check
mise run build
mise run build:rust:tests
mise run test:rust:unit
```

The scaffold uses the explicitly selected Harmos source revision or local checkout.
Install `cargo-harmos` to run `mise run dev`; it is the development tool used to create this project.
Keep generated tooling current with `stkr project update` when adopting company tooling changes.

## Operation Context

Operations consume their request in `run(self, ctx: harmos::Context<'_, Self>)`. The guest SDK re-exports the same
`Operation`, `Context` and `Response` types. Declare `resources` and `operations` on the operation; use
`ctx.resource::<T>()`, `ctx.operation(request)` and `ctx.streams()`. Plugin lifecycle hooks use `harmos_guest::kit::Context`.
